    <!-- Help Dialog -->
    <string name="dialog_help_title">Image Obfuscation Help</string>
    <string name="dialog_help_1">• Obfuscation &amp; Deobfuscation: These are inverse operations. Deobfuscating once reverses one round of obfuscation.</string>
    <string name="dialog_help_2">• Space-filling Curve (Tomato): Based on generalized Hilbert curves and golden-ratio shift, keyless and lossless.</string>
    <string name="dialog_help_3">• PicEncrypt / MD5: Uses chaotic maps or MD5 shuffling. The exact same mode and key must be used to deobfuscate.</string>
    <string name="dialog_help_4">• Restore: Revert to the original image state when imported.</string>
    <string name="dialog_help_5">• Note: Always share the original PNG files. Lossy compression (e.g. non-original image sending in chat apps) will corrupt pixel data and prevent restoration.</string>
    <string name="dialog_got_it">Got it</string>

